{
  "_comment": "§08 — USD per MILLION tokens. Verified against platform.claude.com, developers.openai.com and ai.google.dev. Prices drift: drop a corrected copy at ~/.orangebox/pricing.json and orangebox deep-merges it over this file at boot, no upgrade needed.",
  "_updated": "2026-07-31",
  "_notes": {
    "anthropic_cache": "cache_read is 0.1x input; cache_write is 1.25x input (the 5-minute ephemeral TTL, which is the default). A 1h TTL write costs 2x input — orangebox cannot tell the two apart from the usage object, so it assumes 5m.",
    "openai_cache": "OpenAI cache writes are billed at the normal input rate, so there is no cache_write key. cache_read is listed for completeness; §7.3 does not extract cached-token counts in v1, so it currently goes unused.",
    "sonnet_5_intro": "claude-sonnet-5 has promotional pricing of 2.00 in / 10.00 out through 2026-08-31. The standard rates are listed below so this file stays correct after that date; costs for Sonnet 5 calls made before then are over-estimated by ~33%.",
    "gemini_tiers": "Gemini charges more for prompts over 200k tokens, and 3.6/3.7 Flash carry promotional rates through 2026-12-31. orangebox stores one flat rate per model, so the figures below are the base tier: long-context Gemini calls are under-estimated. Every cost in the UI is labelled \"est.\" for exactly this class of reason.",
    "local_providers": "Ollama and other local runtimes report a cost of 0 rather than an em-dash — there is no per-token bill for a model on your own hardware. That is decided by provider in pricing.mjs, not by a table entry."
  },
